# hotbed / Hotbed — what shipping means
# The repo ships SOURCE ONLY. Big/runtime artifacts are fetched or built on
# the user's machine — see docs/RELEASING.md and install.sh.

# Debian cloud master image — downloaded once at runtime via `hotbedvm fetch-image`
# (~1 GB unpacked, ~330 MB compressed). NEVER commit it.
vm/images/

# Per-VM runtime state: overlay disks, generated seed ISOs, serial captures,
# transient logs. Destroyed with the VM; regenerated by the kit.
vm/vms/

# Scratch convention for multi-GB disk work (see README): probed seeds,
# smoke capture logs. Local only — never commit.
vm/.work/

# Docker volume layout for the hotbedvmd backend (runtime only)
vm/hotbedvmd/store/

# Compiled daemon (release artifact: build via make release / make build,
# attach to GitHub Releases — do not commit binaries)
hotbed/bin/
hotbed/hotbedd

# Release output + local junk
dist/
*.sum
nohup.out
